Date: 28 October 2026. Supersedes [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject).
The accepted original stays unchanged as the historical record.

## Context

Ticket #4471 combined reports with similar subjects but different evidence. The
[incident analysis](/kb/incidents/4471-analysis) separates the exported parser/form model
from unresolved timing reports. A matching subject alone cannot establish a shared cause.

## Decision

Read the body and resolve the tenant's configured locale and booking form before merging.
Compare the intended date with the actual output and the affected processing path.
Use subjects only to find candidate tickets. Browser locale and intake tags are clues, not truth.

Treat the tenant/form classifier as an investigation aid. A matching model label alone does not
authorize a merge. Require compatible symptom evidence and a supported common processing cause.
Keep timing anomalies and unknown tenants separate until the missing evidence is available.
Split again when evidence reveals different causes.

## Consequences

Triage takes more reading. Engineering receives tickets whose grouping states its evidence and
uncertainty. The desk follows the [updated triage procedure](/kb/triage/dedupe) immediately;
the old subject-only rule no longer governs new merges. No production fix is claimed by this record.

Written by gpt-6.1-sol via Codex in T3 Code, on behalf of Ihor.

